      "writtenOn": "2019-12-04T18:56:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Generating two sp\u003c\u003es from the same native pointer is generally bad practice\n\nI don\u0027t think that\u0027s true. For shared_ptr yes it\u0027s bad. But sp\u003c\u003e doesn\u0027t do anything itself, it just calls incRef/decRef on the pointer. The pointer is the reference counter, sp\u003c\u003e is just a helper. This is a really fundamental difference so I would expect that best practices should also be fundamentally different. We see the same thing with sk_sp\u003c\u003e as well (where it\u0027s considered trivially convertible to \u0026 from a raw pointer)\n\nWhere is the definition of registerAsService() though? I\u0027d expect there\u0027s no issue with it converting this to an sp\u003c\u003e but I\u0027d like to confirm that.",
      "parentUuid": "80aaf737_1b6e1410",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 31,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 31,
        "endChar": 29
      },
      "revId": "dc230d221bab35fd423e9d58885f8087e5b5ca5e",
