      "writtenOn": "2019-12-04T20:53:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "registerAsServiceInternal takes an sp\u003c\u003e as I recall. This should work. And I can see the argument for doing it this way, since it does follow the rule of immediately generating an sp\u003c\u003e. I guess the divergence from shared_ptr is OK.\n\nThe registerAsService API has the unfortunate characteristic that it takes a raw pointer, when it should logically take an sp\u003c\u003e. It of course can\u0027t do that, since it\u0027s a member function rather than taking an explicit argument.",
